k. FDA adverse event reports from 1997–2000 documented multiple cases of rhabdomyolysis—including one fatality—from pravastatin–fibrate combinations, further underscoring 吉非贝齐’s role in these events [Data: Relationships (32590, 51175, 16199); Entities (4283, 11873)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"OATP1B1 inhibition as a key mechanism for statin toxicity\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Inhibition of the hepatic transporter OATP1B1 significantly increases systemic exposure to many statins, raising the risk of muscle-related adverse effects including 横纹肌溶解症. 吉非贝齐 and its glucuronide metabolite are confirmed inhibitors of OATP1B1 (and OATP1B3), which explains the pronounced interaction with 西立伐他汀 and other statins. This mechanistic insight has informed clinical guidelines recommending avoidance or dose adjustment when combining OATP1B1 substrates with inhibitors [Data: Relationships (28448, 51175); Entities (2981, 8563, 4283)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"CYP2C8 metabolism links 西立伐他汀 and 横纹肌溶解症 risk\",\n            \"explanation\": \"西立伐他汀 is primarily metabolized by CYP2C8, and co-administration with inhibitors of this enzyme or competing substrates can impair its clearance. Although the primary DDI mechanism with 吉非贝齐 involves OATP1B1 inhibition, CYP2C8 plays a complementary role in the metabolic fate of certain statins. Disruption of this pathway may further contribute to elevated drug levels and subsequent myotoxicity. CYP2C8 itself appears as an indicator entity with multiple supporting records, highlighting its relevance in pharmacogenomic and DDI contexts [Data: Entities (13068, 8563); Relationships (948)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"贝特类 drugs indicated for 高TG血症 but carry muscle toxicity risks with statins\",\n            \"explanation\": \"贝特类 drugs, including 吉非贝齐, are primarily indicated for 高TG血症 and 混合型血脂异常 due to their ability to lower triglycerides and raise HDL-C. However, their combination with statins—while therapeutically rational for mixed dyslipidemia—carries a well-documented risk of 横纹肌损害 and 横纹肌溶解症. Clinical evidence indicates that this risk is not uniform across fibrates; non-吉非贝齐 fibrates like fenofibrate appear to have fewer clinically significant interactions [Data: Relationships (24767, 19378, 16272); Entities (11873, 2673, 1400)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"赛伐他汀 also linked to 横纹肌溶解症 in combination therapy\",\n            \"explanation\": \"赛伐他汀 (another name or variant reference to cerivastatin) is explicitly associated with 横纹肌溶解症, especially when used concomitantly with 吉非贝齐. Documentation notes that Bayer withdrew 赛伐他汀 from the market because of fatal rhabdomyolysis cases arising from such combinations. The drug’s metabolism via both CYP2C8 and CYP3A4 made it particularly susceptible to interactions with inhibitors of these pathways or hepatic transporters [Data: Relationships (16296); Entities (8642, 16323)].\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 8.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community includes drugs with documented fatal adverse reactions due to pharmacokinetic interactions, resulting in market withdrawal and significant clinical safety warnings.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782121443, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1357, "prompt_tokens": 5104, "total_tokens": 6461, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1280}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"西立伐他汀, 吉非贝齐, and Risk of Rhabdomyolysis\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on drug–drug interactions (DDIs) involving lipid-lowering agents—